RG52 Mini portrait panel: flycast's built-in Rotate90 (rend.Rotate90=yes) rotates
the Vulkan present quad 90 degrees, but this panel needs 270 degrees (the opposite
direction). flycast exposes only a single CCW direction, so flip the quad vertex
shader rotation from (y,-x) to (-y,x), turning the 90 into 270.

Only affects rk3562 (rg52mini sets rend.Rotate90=yes; rg43h keeps it =no, so its
non-rotated path is untouched). GL renderer path is unaffected (Vulkan shader only).

diff --git a/core/rend/vulkan/shaders.cpp b/core/rend/vulkan/shaders.cpp
index 9321d08..309664a 100644
--- a/core/rend/vulkan/shaders.cpp
+++ b/core/rend/vulkan/shaders.cpp
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@ void main()
 #if ROTATE == 0
 	gl_Position = vec4(in_pos, 1.0);
 #else
-	gl_Position = vec4(in_pos.y, -in_pos.x, in_pos.z, 1.0);
+	gl_Position = vec4(-in_pos.y, in_pos.x, in_pos.z, 1.0);
 #endif
 	outUV = in_uv;
 }
